# Prisma schema

## When to use
- Edit `backend/prisma/schema.prisma` or add migrations

## Inspect first
- Full schema and `@@map` / `@@index` / relations
- All `prisma.*` usages via grep in `backend/src/repositories` and routes
- Whether data is legacy paper (`Account`) vs testnet (`TestnetAccount`)

## Steps
1. Update schema with explicit types; add `@@index` for filtered query patterns (`coin`, `method_id`, `timestamp`).
2. Run `cd backend && npx prisma migrate dev --name <short_name>` to create migration SQL.
3. Run `npm run prisma:generate` (also part of `npm run build`).
4. Update repositories first, then services/routes.
5. Update `docs/api-spec.md` only if public contract changes.

## Rules
- Postgres provider only; `DATABASE_URL` required in production
- Prefer nullable new columns or defaults for backward-compatible deploys
- Cascade deletes already defined on relations — preserve semantics when adding FKs
- snake_case in DB via `@map` / `@@map` when matching existing tables

## Verification
- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds
- [ ] `prisma studio` or sample query against new fields
- [ ] Integration tests or manual API read/write on affected models
